# Never fake FPGA-SIM

F9 FPGA-SIM **is** the chip in Verilator: same `rtl/*.sv` as
`make -C tools/board_flow bit`. Default: `runtime/sim_backend.py`. GUI shows
`FPGA-SIM (RTL)` vs `(HOST)`. Host twin (`JMR_SIM_HOST=1`) is opt-in debug
only — never a quiet fallback when the RTL binary is missing (fail loud:
`make -C sim sim_server_synth`). Do not pretend PYTHON is FPGA-SIM.

Legal SRAM first, then glass. Do not make a title playable on a
Verilator-only heap and “flatten later.” The user runs `make bit` — **never
the agent.** Do not start Vivado to check. Inspect **both** exec32 and
exec64 (titles on 64 still synthesize 32). `sim_server_synth` PASS is not a
bitstream.

Glass is **640×480** (GUI mirror matches HDMI, not a 16-line strip).
Keyboard is **full JS** (case + punctuation); do not reintroduce an a–z fold.

**Legal SRAM:** 1-D array, scalar `we` + wdata, **rdata next clock**, 1 write +
1–2 reads. Dump/tether shares the CPU read port (not a third port). True
dual-port only for CPU+scanout (VRAM / FB). Slot scans are FSMs, one index
per clock, **stop at `vobj_len` / `venv_len`**, not always 32. Operand stack
is 1W1R registered (not combo/multi-port LUTRAM). Extra GET_PROP clocks are
silicon (~30 MHz). Caps (same in PYTHON): `MAX_OBJ=1024`, arrays
`1536×32+128×128`, `ENV_DEPTH=512`. Do not restore `8192`/`4096` (~7 MB).
Overflow loud. JS heap is not the 4 MB ASET bank; do not bump that bank to
8 MB. `cls_*` 16×16 (4 Kbit) stays. Copy `storage_engine.sv` `sbuf` /
`jmr_video_vram.sv` Port A. Fit numbers:
[docs/FPGA_FIT.md](../../docs/FPGA_FIT.md). Live leftovers:
[docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md](../../docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md).

## Six rules (do not ship a diff that breaks one)

1. **One copy, one owner.** Parent holds the tables. Exec: address in, data
   next clock. Do not clone `stack` / `vvars` / `name_mem` / `intern_var` /
   `cstack` / `json_mem` into exec to dodge a port (`one-heap-keep-gen`).

2. **The opcode `always_comb` assigns no ports.** It writes local `*_n` and
   local we/addr only. Parent sees `*_q` (clocked in exec). Any combo output
   of that block — used `stack_we`, unused `foo_n`, even `raddr = sp-1` at
   the top — is one cone; Vivado flattens exec into the parent.
   `keep_hierarchy` does not save it. raddr that is only registered `sp` /
   TOS / `code_rdata` belongs in a **separate** `assign` outside that block.

3. **No combo `arr[i]`.** Not in `always_comb`, `assign`, or
   `function automatic` (no TOS/SRAM peek from the opcode case — that is a
   registered window or `*_rdata`, not a third port). Decoder reads
   `*_rdata`. No 2-D heap tables. No whole-array combo copy
   (`to_fn_n[i] = to_fn[i]`). No `for (k) if (mem[k]==key)` CAM — a `for`
   over slots in `always_ff` is N parallel compares, not N clocks; that is
   an FSM. No `for (i = j; i < N)` — write `for (i = 0; i < N) if (i >= j)`.
   No nested `for` over `ENV_DEPTH`. No reset/`p_clr` `for` that writes
   every cell in one cycle.

4. **Ports are scalars or packed vectors.** Unpacked array ports flatten
   (even unused). No nested `bus[a:b][c:d]` (packed-slice part-select, e.g.
   `rdata[79:64][9:0]` or `pack[i +: 64][11:0]`). Unpack once to a 64-bit
   wire, then `wire[11:0]` (or use `rdata[73:64]`).

5. **Plain `case` on opcode and `nid`.** `unique case` on those two is every
   arm in parallel. Small `unique case (state)` / `(p_sel)` stays.

6. **Do not fake the chip.** No `` `ifdef SYNTHESIS `` smaller heap, no
   `RAMB36` inside the VM, no sim-sized depths (~7 MB). Last unused-FF print
   (`e32_p_clr_reg was removed`, 8-3936 trim) is not the cause — RSS climbing
   after a frozen log is flatten. Kill that; fix rules 2–3 by inspection.

```systemverilog
// BAD — combo index, combo port, one cone with the opcode case
always_comb begin
  stack_raddr = sp - 1;          // still a port of the giant comb
  vars_raddr = intern_var[idx];  // 1024-mux on a port
  unique case (opcode) … stack_we = 1; endcase
end
// GOOD — locals in the case; raddr outside; parent sees *_q
assign stack_raddr = (sp >= 1) ? (sp - 1) : 0;
always_comb begin
  stack_we = 1'b0;  // local
  case (opcode) … stack_we = 1'b1; endcase
end
always_ff @(posedge clk) stack_we_q <= stack_we;
```
